    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3b29a974_40686020",
        "filename": "chip/max32660/uart_chip.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 250,
      "author": {
        "id": 1341996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-06T18:57:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The approach here seems to differ from the way that alternate functions of IO pins are configured on other chips in the EC codebase.\n\nUsually, if there is a choice of multiple pins to use for one UART, that choice is made through the ALTERNATE() macro in gpio.inc, and uart_init() would invoke gpio_config_module(MODULE_UART) at some point, to configure those pins.\n\nI think that uart_gpio_configure() needs to be removed, and replaced with proper use of ALTERNATE() in gpio.inc.",
      "revId": "35217913716aaeb0939615858c8987fd19734d1c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "78c60dcf_a17b6071",
        "filename": "chip/max32660/uart_chip.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 347,
      "author": {
        "id": 1341996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-06T18:57:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The EC is generally space constrained, so we do not want to include more code abstractions than necessary.\n\nWe support only one UART and which one it is is declared in a define UARTN.\n\nIf you look at e.g. ec/chip/stm32/uart.c, you will see that its code uses a series of #ifdef such that when compiling the EC code with any particular value of UARTN, then only the register addresses relevant to that particular uart gets compiled into the code.\n\nThis file on the other hand, has a bunch of methods which take uart number as an integer in their parameters, and do a table lookup using MXC_UART_GET_UART, meaning that any compiled EC image would have to include a table with addresses of all the UARTS in the chip, even all the ones that are not used.\n\nIdeally, I would like to see the mxc_uart_regs_t struct gone from the code.",
      "revId": "35217913716aaeb0939615858c8987fd19734d1c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
